## 1) Architecture & State Management
- Use Riverpod exclusively (`flutter_riverpod`). Prefer `StateNotifierProvider` for state with actions.
- Keep widgets pure; move IO/business logic to providers/services.
- Providers live under `lib/src/features/<feature>/providers/` and are named `*_provider.dart`.
- Model classes go in `.../models/` and are immutable. Use `freezed`/`json_serializable` where helpful.
- Avoid global singletons. Inject via providers.

Example pattern:
```dart
class AuthState {
  final bool isLoading;
  final User? user;
  final String? error;
  const AuthState({this.isLoading = false, this.user, this.error});
}

class AuthNotifier extends StateNotifier<AuthState> {
  AuthNotifier(this._api) : super(const AuthState());
  final ApiService _api;

  Future<void> login(String email, String password) async {
    state = AuthState(isLoading: true);
    try {
      final user = await _api.login(email, password);
      state = AuthState(user: user);
    } catch (e) {
      state = AuthState(error: e.toString());
    }
  }
}
```

## 2) Navigation & Routing
- Use `go_router` only, centralized in `lib/src/core/routing/app_router.dart`.
- Use `context.go(...)` for top-level changes; `context.push(...)` for drill-ins.
- Do not call `Navigator.of(context).push` directly.
- Add guards/redirects in the router, not inside leaf widgets.
- Use `rootNavigatorKey` for app-wide overlays.

## 3) Theme & Styling
- Use `AppTheme` (Material 3 enabled). Do not hardcode colors or font sizes.
- Use tokens from `AppColors`, `AppDimensions`, `AppTypography`.
- Derive colors/typography from `Theme.of(context)` when possible.
- Spacing: follow 8pt grid via `AppDimensions`. Radii and elevations from tokens.

Correct usage:
```dart
Text('Title', style: Theme.of(context).textTheme.headlineMedium);
Container(color: Theme.of(context).colorScheme.primary);
```

Avoid:
```dart
Text('Title', style: TextStyle(fontSize: 24));
Container(color: Colors.blue);
```

## 4) Inputs & Forms
- Use shared components: `CustomTextField`, `PasswordField` under `src/components/inputs/`.
- Wrap related inputs in a `Form` with `GlobalKey<FormState>` and synchronous validators.
- Keyboard & focus:
  - Set `keyboardType`, `textInputAction` (next/done), and `inputFormatters`.
  - On next: advance focus. On done: `FocusScope.of(context).unfocus()`.
  - Ensure content is scrollable and keyboard-safe.
- Accessibility:
  - Provide `label` and `hint`. Respect `maxLength` and show counters as needed.
- Loading/disabled: disable submit buttons during async submits; show spinner in-button.

## 5) Modals, Sheets, Overlays
- Use `showDialog` with a shaped `Dialog` (≥ 16px radius), padding 24px, and clear header/content/actions.
- Bottom sheets via `showModalBottomSheet` with:
  - `isScrollControlled: true`, `useSafeArea: true`
  - `backgroundColor: Theme.of(context).colorScheme.surface`
  - Rounded top shape (≥ 16px)
  - Provide visible drag handle, sticky header/title, scrollable content, persistent action bar.
- All global overlays must anchor to `rootNavigatorKey`.

Bottom sheet helper:
```dart
await showModalBottomSheet(
  context: context,
  isScrollControlled: true,
  useSafeArea: true,
  backgroundColor: Theme.of(context).colorScheme.surface,
  shape: const RoundedRectangleBorder(
    borderRadius: BorderRadius.vertical(top: Radius.circular(16)),
  ),
  builder: (context) => Padding(
    padding: const EdgeInsets.only(bottom: 16),
    child: child,
  ),
);
```

## 6) Error Handling & Feedback
- Providers/services return explicit error messages. No silent failures.
- Surface results using themed snackbars/toasts and optional haptics.
- For form errors, show inline helper/error text near the input.

## 7) Performance & Memory
- Prefer `const` constructors, pure widgets, and builder patterns for lists.
- Debounce rapid input-driven network calls.
- Dispose controllers/animations in `dispose()`.
- Avoid heavy work in `build`; move to providers.
- Use `CachedNetworkImage` for remote images.

## 8) Accessibility
- Touch targets ≥ 44x44dp.
- Sufficient contrast using theme tokens.
- Provide semantics labels for icon-only actions.
- Support text scaling. Avoid clipped text; use flexible layouts and `maxLines` judiciously.
- Avoid focus traps in modals; support back button and barrier dismiss for non-destructive flows.

## 9) Networking & Services
- All HTTP calls go through `lib/src/core/services/api_service.dart` or feature services.
- Do not call HTTP directly from widgets.
- Providers own request state (loading/error/data). Widgets subscribe and render accordingly.
- Use secure storage for tokens (`flutter_secure_storage`).

## 10) Code Organization & Naming
- Screens: `.../screens/*_screen.dart`
- Dialogs: `.../*_dialog.dart`
- Bottom sheets: `.../*_sheet.dart`
- Providers: `.../*_provider.dart`
- Shared components: `lib/src/components/`
- Shared utilities: `lib/src/core/utils/`

Naming:
- Files: `snake_case.dart`
- Classes: `PascalCase`
- Variables: `camelCase`
- Constants: `UPPER_SNAKE_CASE`
- Private members: `_camelCase`

## 11) Testing
- Widget tests for forms/dialogs/sheets covering validation, disabled states, and navigation intents.
- Provider tests for state transitions and error paths.
- Golden tests for critical screens with `AppTheme.lightTheme`.
- No new lint warnings; tests must pass before PR.

## 12) Checklists

Before Starting
- [ ] Confirm API contracts and designs
- [ ] Define models and providers
- [ ] Identify navigation routes and guards

For Each Screen
- [ ] Responsive layout, keyboard safe
- [ ] Uses shared inputs and AppTheme tokens
- [ ] Loading, error, empty states
- [ ] Accessibility labels and semantics
- [ ] Navigation via `go_router`

Before PR
- [ ] No lint warnings
- [ ] Unit/widget tests added and passing
- [ ] Performance sanity check
- [ ] Screenshots for major UI
- [ ] Docs updated where needed

